\section{Conclusion}
Adding the observed mean residual $b=3$ removes the fixed predictor's constant offset on the five supplied observations. The measured error table and two figures connect the numerical calculation to its data dependencies and evaluation scope. Exact agreement follows from the constant residual vector and reuse of the observations. The calculation supports no conclusion about unseen observations; any assessment of transfer remains outside the supplied evidence.

